    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **62 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (which handles `POST /api/owners`).\n\n**The change:**\n1. Injected `HttpServletRequest` into the controller so the optional `Idempotency-Key` header can be read (the `addOwner` signature comes from the OpenAPI-generated `OwnersApi` interface and can't take a new parameter, so reading it off the request is the least-invasive approach).\n2. Added an `idempotentCreates` map (`ConcurrentHashMap<String, Integer>`) recording, per key, the id of the owner originally created.\n3. In `addOwner`:\n   - **Before** any validation/duplicate checks, if the request carries a non-blank `Idempotency-Key` that has already been seen, it fetches the originally created owner and returns it with **200 OK** \u2014 bypassing the duplicate-identity check that would otherwise return 409.\n   - After a successful create, it records `key \u2192 owner.getId()` so a later repeat with the same key resolves to the original owner. First creates still return **201 Created** as before.\n\nRequests without the header behave exactly as before. The acceptance test `Cp50Tests.coreIdempotentRepeat` (first call `2xx`, repeat `200`, same id) passes, and all 62 tests remain green.",
