    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list for **POST /api/owners** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, request body `OwnerFieldsDto`).\n\n## Before the controller body runs\n\n1. **Bean Validation** on `OwnerFieldsDto` (triggered by `@Valid` on the API interface). Constraints:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(max 10)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)` (nullable)\n   - `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)` (nullable)\n\n   A failure here \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400**.\n\n## Inside the controller (in exact execution order)\n\n2. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` header was seen before, return the previously-created owner (**200 OK**) and skip everything below.\n3. **`normalizeAddress`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 composes/normalizes address lines (upper-case, collapse whitespace, expand ST/RD/AVE), writes back to `address`.\n4. **`validateRequiredFields`** \u2014 firstName / lastName / address / city / telephone must be non-blank \u2192 else `RequiredFieldsMissingException` (**400**).\n5. **`validatePostcode`** \u2014 if present, region range check \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (**400**).\n6. **`normalizeTelephone`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 convert to E.164, write back; invalid \u2192 `RequiredFieldsMissingException` (**400**).\n7. **`normalizeEmail`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 if present, syntax + disposable-domain check, lower-case, write back \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (**400**).\n8. **`rejectDuplicateIdentity`** \u2014 identityKey (`tel|email|householdId`) vs existing non-deleted owners \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**).\n9. **`rejectDuplicateHousehold`** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold=true`, householdId collision \u2192 `DuplicateHouseholdException` (**409**).\n10. **`rejectCityAtCapacity`** \u2014 \u2265 50 owners in the city \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n11. **`rejectFutureRegistrationDate`** \u2014 supplied date after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (**400**).\n12. **`defaultRegistrationDate`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 default to today if null, then roll weekend/holiday forward to next business day; write back.\n13. **`rejectDailyLimit`** \u2014 \u2265 100 owners on that business day \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` (**429**).\n14. **`ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)`** \u2014 MapStruct maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity (ignores `id` and `pets`).\n15. **Derived-field assignment** *(all side-effects on the entity, pre-persist)*:\n    - `assignCustomerCode` (SHA-256 of tel+lastName, region prefix, de-duped)\n    - `assignHouseholdId` (SHA-256 of lastName|postcode)\n    - `assignHouseholdMemberCount`\n    - `assignNamesakeCount`\n    - `assignMembershipNumber`\n    - `assignBulkSignupWarning` (> 80 signups/day)\n    - `assignPossibleDuplicate` (flag + `possibleDuplicateOf`)\n16. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `@Transactional`, persists via the repository (`save`). No JPA lifecycle callbacks, entity listeners, or auditing exist.\n17. **Record idempotency key** *(side-effect)* \u2014 store `key \u2192 owner.id` in the in-memory `idempotentCreates` map.\n18. **Audit log** *(side-effect)* \u2014 the `\"AUDIT\"` SLF4J logger emits an info line (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber).\n19. **`ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)`** \u2014 build response (fills transient/derived getters: salutation, membership level/points, locality/timezone, etc.).\n20. **Set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`** header and return **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Important caveats\n\n- **All the business validation (steps 4\u201313) is hand-written imperative code in the controller**, not JSR-380 validators and not in the service layer. `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` does nothing but call `ownerRepository.save`.\n- The **entity `Owner` also carries its own constraints** (`@NotEmpty` firstName/lastName/address/city, `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)` telephone), but these apply to the entity, not to request binding.\n- **Security is disabled by default**: `petclinic.security.enable=false`, so the `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN)\")` on the handler is **not enforced** unless the flag is turned on (which activates `@EnableMethodSecurity`).\n- Several of the uniqueness/derived helpers each call `findAllOwners()` \u2014 multiple full-table scans per create.\n\nNo changes were made to the code."
